# .gitignore — KokertechAI
# Created 2026-09-21 (Sprint 19.8 audit); git initialized 2026-09-22
# (Sprint 19.8.3 — the audit's #1 systemic-risk item closed). Large
# binaries, secrets, and ephemera must never enter history: a repo can
# un-commit, but it cannot un-leak.

# --- Secrets (CRITICAL: KOKERTECH_API_KEY lives here) ---
.env

# --- Databases (5+ GB vault, WAL sidecars, orphan DBs) ---
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal

# --- Large binaries (12 GB models, 290 MB voices, 111 MB backups) ---
models/
voice_models/
Backups/
settings_backups/

# --- Python runtime artifacts ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
.tox/

# --- Virtual environments ---
.venv/
venv/

# --- Node (vscode-freebuff-agents build tree) ---
node_modules/
out/

# --- Ephemeral project output / diagnostics / runs ---
_runs/
_diag/
_scratch/
.scratch/
.sessions/
execution_log.txt
_pytest_full_output.txt
session_journal.jsonl

# --- Editor / OS noise ---
.vs/
.vscode/
.claude/settings.local.json
desktop.ini
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store

# --- AI assistant workspaces (ephemeral state) ---
.blackbox/
.blackboxcli/
.fsc/
.claude/
.agents/

# --- Runtime-mutated state (recreated by the app on every run) ---
user_identity.json
openclaw-workspace-state.json
data/resource_history.json

# --- Forensic leftovers (recovery saga, 2026-07) ---
*.py.corrupted

# --- Build artifacts (rebuilt by build scripts; never history) ---
build/
dist/
*.spec
/KokertechAi.exe
/KokertechAi.pdb
*.pdb

# Live-app runtime state (mutated continuously by the running app / client)
data/chat_history.json
data/screenshots/
data/logs/
.freebuff/
context_summary.txt
data/logs/.save_complete
data/screenshots/

# --- pytest runtime artifacts ---
tests/_test_*.txt

# --- Ephemeral audit logs & local test files ---
data/tool_execution_audit.jsonl
*.zip
testKai.txt

# --- Personal assistant workspace (private context: never published) ---
# Untracked 2026-10-07, before this repo was switched to public. These hold
# the owner's profile, session logs, and curated long-term memory, so they
# stay local-only. scripts/assert_doc_drift.py reads SOUL.md/IDENTITY.md
# from disk and skips absent files, so keeping them present but untracked
# keeps that gate green.
/MEMORY.md
/USER.md
/SOUL.md
/IDENTITY.md
/memory/
/AGENTS.md
/TOOLS.md

# --- Internal working docs (not published) ---
# Untracked 2026-10-07 when the repo was reduced to source + README. The
# files stay ON DISK and are NOT deleted: scripts/assert_no_corrupted_files.py
# (Gate 9) reads recovery_manifest.md from the filesystem and hard-fails when
# it is absent, and scripts/assert_doc_drift.py / check_knowledge_anchors.py
# .glob() these directories and tolerate their absence. Untracking keeps the
# gate suite green while publishing nothing.
/docs/
/save_session.md
/HEARTBEAT.md
/recovery_manifest.md
/recovery_resolution_20260722.md

# --- Personal data (untracked 2026-10-09) ---
# app_settings.json carries the owner's name/background/preferences; these are
# user-generated state, kept on disk but never published.
app_settings.json
custom_themes.json
personas.json

# --- Runtime data tree (recreated by the app on every run) ---
data/

# --- Local decompile/build tooling ---
tools/

# --- Office documents ---
*.docx

# --- Internal project docs, kept local-only (not published) ---
/CONTEXT.md
/KNOWN_FAILURES.md
/TOOL_USAGE_RULES.md
